WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:02.542
(soft music)

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.430
- Greetings,

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.200
and welcome to this celebration

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.523
of the Yale School of
Nursing, Class of 2020.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.300
It's an honor to be able to share

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.370
in this special day with you

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.750
and to commemorate this
important milestone.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.140
While we are sad, we cannot be together

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.410
for our usual festivities, in New Haven.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.200
I am grateful that we can
gather virtually across space

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.333
and time, to mark the occasion.

00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:35.780
Let me begin by thanking
all those watching,

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.040
loved ones, faculty, staff,

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.520
and mentors who have supported
our extraordinary graduates

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.870
during their time at YSN, as
they work to become the nurses,

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.780
midwives, health system leaders,

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.210
and nurse scientists

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.453
that the world is desperately
calling for, right now.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.710
Congratulations to every
single one of our graduates

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.303
on crossing this finish
line, albeit virtually.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:04.220
It's an understatement

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:05.840
to say that the world
was a different place

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.150
when you started at Yale School
of Nursing those years ago.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.350
It was different even
just a few months ago.

00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:16.310
Some of you had only just
begun your nursing journey

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.700
while, others came to YSN

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.370
to build on years of nursing experience.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.470
You had clear goals

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.320
and an inspired vision

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.303
for how your education would progress.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.140
In any journey, bumps on the
road can be expected, assessed

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.050
and dealt with accordingly.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.723
And often these bumps lead
to the greatest growth,

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.410
a clinical rotation may alter
the direction of a career,

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.690
a professor's comment may
inspire a new research thread,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:45.193
and a project may launch a movement.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.923
No matter how you started, you
are finishing as Yale nurses.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.163
You answered when the world called.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.780
You've handled your last semester

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.060
with grace, grit, flexibility

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.540
and determination

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.473
and you are to be applauded for that.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.030
From here you will set forth as a healer

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:10.673
at a time when society is
facing unprecedented need.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:17.800
No simulation has prepared the
world for COVID-19's impact,

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.080
but I trust that you can take
everything you learned at YSN

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.080
coupled with the different
experiences you brought with you

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.400
and help lead your
communities out of a pandemic

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.730
that has made clear societies
disparities, weaknesses

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:31.753
and fragilities.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.880
The COVID-19 pandemic will remake us

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:41.750
and Yale nurses must help
remake society to be more just

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.390
through your work in the
health systems, universities,

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.493
and other workplaces across the country.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.280
As Yale nurses, you will
be joining communities

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.163
and institutions that
need you more than ever.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.120
Congratulations Class of
2020, we are so proud of you.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.537
(soft music)

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.143
I am honored now

00:03:07.143 --> 00:03:10.070
to recognize exceptional
individuals from our community

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:12.450
who have been nominated
by students and faculty,

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.890
for teaching, scholarship,
service, and research

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:18.053
through our annual recognition process.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.900
Annie Goodrich, the founding
dean of Yale School of Nursing,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.490
was an outstanding nurse leader

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:25.323
and educator,

00:03:25.323 --> 00:03:28.310
whose vision set the course
for nursing education.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:31.630
The very origins of our
school emerged from the ashes

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:35.510
of another worldwide
conflagration, World War I.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.040
We honor her legacy through
the Annie Goodrich Award

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.930
for excellence in teaching,

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:45.250
by recognizing a faculty member
who carries on the tradition

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.053
of exceptional nursing education.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.990
Each year, students
nominate faculty members

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:53.510
highlighting their
outstanding teaching skills,

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.830
professional activities

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:57.970
and effectiveness as a
role model, availability

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.690
and support for students

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.023
and community activities.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.640
This year's recipient
exemplifies nursing excellence

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.603
through her commitment to all students.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.560
During the COVID-19 outbreak,

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.579
she recognized a need
for a change in seminar.

00:04:12.579 --> 00:04:15.010
She created a space for students

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.940
to talk about their concerns
with their jobs, homes,

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.793
and families.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.800
She started each stone call
with a mindfulness exercise

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.110
and encouraged students to bring exercises

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.960
they could facilitate with the group.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:29.100
As a preceptor liaison,

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.100
she has built many trusting relationships

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.050
with clinicians in the community

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.220
and is working to spread

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:37.610
YSN Psychiatric-Mental Health
Nurse Practitioner students,

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.260
through different levels of care.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.220
She is also an instructor
who teaches across programs

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.230
and has transformed
the teaching experience

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.853
and classroom space for the GEPN students.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.440
This year, we're proud
to present the 2020,

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.130
Annie Goodrich Award for
excellence in teaching

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:57.200
to an amazing advisor,
faculty member and mentor,

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.090
Dr. Dilice Robertson.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:00.010
Congratulations,

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.843
and thank you, Dr. Robertson.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.610
The Charles King Jr
Memorial Scholars Aid Prize

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.290
is given to a graduating student

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.590
who has demonstrated
outstanding performance

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:13.960
in scholarship, research

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.660
and clinical practice

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.133
and who through accomplishments

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:20.040
in leadership of all aspects of study

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:23.573
has inspired an admiration
for professional nursing work.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.580
The recipient has proven herself

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.723
to be the quintessential APRN to be.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:32.140
She actively sought out
experiences in community health

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.320
through her volunteerism
at the HAVEN Free Clinic

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.410
through her request for

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:37.990
and completion of a rotation

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:39.990
with the Yale Community Health Care Van.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.720
Through her participation
in the gender, sexuality

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.960
and health justice concentration

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:47.980
and through her work in Tijuana, Mexico

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.060
providing prenatal care, primary care

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:51.240
and other services

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.683
with the Refugee Health
Alliances Organization.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:57.210
She is compassionate, astute

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.500
and approachable to all individuals
with whom she interacts.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.660
She continues to be a
leader in nursing knowledge

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.890
through her work as a MedSurg Nursing TA,

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.210
her ongoing work

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:08.770
with the Minority Student
Nurses Organization

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.030
and in her professional life,

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:13.310
serving on behalf of
underserved populations.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.840
And she embodies forward-looking action

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.260
as she said about another
celebration, the GEPN graduation.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.630
Our work here, as nurses, students

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:24.415
and activists, is just beginning.

00:06:24.415 --> 00:06:26.270
It's a great pleasure to award

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:29.318
the 2020 Charles King Jr.
Memorial Scholars Aid Prize

00:06:29.318 --> 00:06:31.640
to Camille Lawhead,

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.493
Congratulations, Miss Lawhead.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.330
The Milton and Ann Sidney Prize,

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.060
is awarded to a graduating student

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.680
whose research in the
judgment of the faculty

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.280
best exemplifies the school's commitment

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.320
to clinical scholarship

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.440
and its mission to
contribute to better health

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:49.503
for all people.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.280
This year's recipient has
produced an in depth exploration

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.450
of vaginal birth after
cesarean section, VBAC

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.763
in the United States.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:02.210
Her integrative review,
expose the facilitators

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.270
and barriers identified in the literature

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:06.340
of accessing VBAC in the U.S.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.640
Her study of 2017 birth certificate data

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.290
is the first large dataset,

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.470
state by state demographic

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.743
and geographic examination of VBAC.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.690
Her mixed methods, dissertation research,

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:21.150
uncovered graphic stories
of women's struggles

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.980
to have vaginal birth
after birth caesarean,

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.230
sometimes forcing them into unsafe choices

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:29.200
such as giving birth in a
hotel room near a hospital

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.600
that would not let them
labor in their facility.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.340
She found that women who felt disrespected

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:37.333
or lacked autonomy, were
less likely to plan a VBAC.

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:40.390
This nominee has six national

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.480
and international presentations or posters

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.023
during her doctoral program.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.020
Her dissertation research was supported

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.137
by the March of Dimes
Margaret Comerford Freda,

00:07:49.137 --> 00:07:51.250
"Saving Babies Together Award."

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.710
The Association of
Women's Health Obstetric

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:55.330
and Neonatal Nurses

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.000
and the Rockefeller university
Heilbrunn Family Center

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.173
for Nursing Research.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.890
Noting the depth and care for work,

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:06.120
I am honored to award the
Milton and Ann Sidney Prize

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.403
to Dr. Bridget Lynn Basile Ibrahim.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.013
Congratulations, Dr. Ibrahim.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:15.380
It's now my pleasure

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:18.330
to introduce one of our
graduating students, Danielle Um,

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.410
in the Adult-Gerontology Primary Care

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.860
Nurse Practitioner Specialty,

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.630
who will address the Class of 2020.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:28.640
- I still remember the first
day I stepped into YSN.

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:31.240
A little excited, a little nervous,

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.060
and very much determined.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.220
I was, however, Yale headed

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:36.430
that my parents bought
me to congratulate me

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.800
on getting accepted to the program.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.150
Also at orientation, I remember
twirling my hoodie strings

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:45.100
and thinking in my mind of
what to say to my new peers

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:47.050
so as to not make a fool out of myself.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:48.760
First introductions

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.260
and a bit of awkwardness,

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:51.720
is now something I can look back on

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.433
and laugh about my cohort
who are now my friends.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.170
We have all come a long way,

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:58.960
fought for our own struggles

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:02.560
and managed to make it to the
finish line, hand in hand.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.573
So where do we go from here?

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:07.702
Some of us will continue
our journey in academics

00:09:07.702 --> 00:09:11.450
following the footsteps of
our DNP and PhD colleagues

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.900
earning doctoral degrees,

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.240
becoming researchers and professors.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.640
Some of us may dive back
into the clinical field

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.660
working as advanced practice
nurses of private practices

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.105
or university hospitals

00:09:22.105 --> 00:09:24.580
or maybe for working for the CDC.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.163
I hear they’re busy these days.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.420
The possibilities are
almost dauntingly unless,

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.800
but no matter what we all
decide to do with our degrees,

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.333
there is one common point.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:38.070
What will ties together
is the shared heritage

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.960
and the practice of nursing.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:42.210
We are all about to embark on careers

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:46.070
that require the highest levels
of empathy and compassion.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:51.010
We're committed, selfless, unified, brave

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:53.490
and fierce multitaskers.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.010
This is the common point

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.610
that I've seen at every
single one of my classmates.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.870
Alongside our fellow healthcare providers

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:03.950
in various specialties,
we tested our strengths

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.993
during these unprecedented times
with the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.770
We volunteered at local clinics.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:13.793
We work long, seemingly
hopeless shifts in the ICU.

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.130
We helped with hotline calls

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:18.530
from terrified potential patients.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.490
We video chatted our friends and family

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:21.323
her questions

00:10:21.323 --> 00:10:23.123
and concerns about possible symptoms.

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:26.420
We came together as a community

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:28.690
to get their commencement cancellations.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.610
We shared resources and knowledge,

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:32.163
and reached out to one another.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.640
Through it all, we have become more aware

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:37.600
of what's at stake

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.240
and we have proved resilient

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.830
and knit together even closer.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.470
We're the grassroots, we're the heartbeat,

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.743
we're the frontline
warriors, the mast army.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:55.420
As Yale nurses, may we never
forget where we started,

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.170
where we come from.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.560
Let us also not forget our sense of pride

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.151
and this honorable call of duty

00:11:01.151 --> 00:11:03.283
that fills us all with fire, today.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.920
More than ever, the field
of nursing has become vital

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:08.270
in healthcare

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.160
and the demand for nursing professionals

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.070
in the United States alone,

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:15.520
is expected to increase
drastically in the coming years.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.650
We're facing our time when our expertise

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.670
and dedication, is desperately
needed at hospitals

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:24.050
and clinics all over the world.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:26.200
And now it is our turn to step up

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.583
and fully embrace these responsibilities.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.230
As we go out into the real world,

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:33.470
with all training wheels off,

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:36.300
may we not be afraid to step
out of our comfort zones,

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:39.280
may we be willing to work
in underserved communities

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.487
and may we never forget why YSN's mission,

00:11:41.487 --> 00:11:43.247
"Better health for all people."

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:47.170
I like to close by giving
thanks to where they are do.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:49.390
First, to our amazing YSN staff

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:52.170
who put up with our endless
emails and questions

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:54.570
and solves all of our difficulties,

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:57.500
to our professors who
have guided us so far

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:00.710
and taught us what it takes
to become a true Yale nurse.

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:02.770
To our family and loved ones,

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:05.570
thank you, for your
unconditional love and support.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:08.860
We would not have been able
to do this without you.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:10.810
And to our peers, who pushed

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:13.440
and motivated each other
to keep faith in the vision

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:14.853
and trust the process.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:19.260
In the future, when we look
back at our time at YSN,

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:20.870
from texting your friend every morning

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.970
asking them what classroom to go to,

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.780
forgetting your student ID
to get into the building,

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:28.780
talking about what our future
holds for us in the hub,

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:31.060
celebrating the end of every semester

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.083
and studying in the study
rooms for hours on end.

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.610
I hope that those memories bring you joy

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.730
and most importantly, I
hope they keep you grounded

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:44.000
and motivate you to work
together, appreciate others

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.520
and learn more in order
to be the best you can be

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:47.663
for your patients.

00:12:48.601 --> 00:12:50.510
As someone quoted Nightingale,

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:53.100
on the white board, on
the ground floor of YSN,

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.940
“let us never consider
ourselves finished nurses

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:58.630
for we must be learning all of our lives.”

